      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T03:19:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a marching crossing within 1e-6 of a sample sits on it (#4107)\n\nA field value a few picometres from zero (a cut floor on the lattice of\ncell centres) put a marching-tetrahedra crossing that close to the\nsample. The facets sharing it kept two corners under the 1e-9 weld, so\nafter the weld (or an f32 export) they collapsed and their neighbours'\nedges sat on three or more facets. On the sample they are exactly\nzero-area and `push` drops them.\n\nPin (crates/sim/tests/iso_node_floor.rs, synthetic): a floor on the\nlattice meshes by marching tetrahedra with 0 collapsed facets and every\nwelded edge on two facets (before: 11,394 collapsed, 5,799 edges); a\nfloor off the lattice stays valid by both methods. Decision:\ndocs/decisions/4107-marching-node-snap.md.\n\nFixes #4107\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
