  {
    "sha": "503d97b3efcfbf7305ae19264ffe055b88a453f8",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV5OD-doAKDUwM2Q5N2IzZWZjZmJmNzMwNWFlMTkyNjRmZmUwNTViODhhNDUzZjg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T05:15:25Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T05:15:25Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the #4107 snap reads the values, so both ends of an edge agree; pins join stock_dual\n\nReview of the first form: it tested the fraction t against 1e-6. The two\ntetrahedra that share an edge cross it from opposite ends and get t and\n1 - t only up to rounding, so near the threshold one snapped and its\nneighbour did not, and their corners stood 1e-6 of an edge apart. The\nsnap now reads |da| and |db| against |da - db|, which are the same numbers\nfrom either end. New unit test\nan_edge_gets_the_same_corner_from_either_end_at_the_snap_threshold fails on\nthe first form (one value of 8,000 near the threshold) and passes now.\n\nThe two pins move from a new test binary into the existing stock_dual\nsuite, which already covers stock_sim::iso (AGENTS.md: new tests join an\nexisting suite, #3187). Wording: the crossing sat about 1e-12 mm from the\nsample (not picometres); the decision file says so and names the f32 case\nthis does not cover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
