        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T05:33:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a snapped #4107 corner is the sample itself\n\nSecond review: a corner snapped to the far sample was computed as\npa + (pb - pa), which beside a coordinate's rounding residue is not pb, so\nin the two-in, two-out case the two facets reaching that sample could keep\na sliver one ulp wide that collapses at the weld. The crossing now returns\nthe sample. Unit test a_snapped_corner_is_the_sample_itself fails on the\nprevious head and passes now. The largest corner move at a 0.25 mm step is\n0.43 nm (a body diagonal), not 0.25 nm.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
